5,Disa in Chad people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/18816,"The Disa people speak a language from the Nilo-Saharan family, which connects them to other ethnic groups in the Sahel region. Their history is rooted in the savanna and semi-arid zones of Chad, where they have lived for generations as part of small, rural communities.",Disa,Nilo-Saharan
